3. Understanding the attack model

Attack types (Table 1) in VeReMi: 

Physical Layer Plausibility Che…

Type 1 – Constant Position: attacker broadcasts a fixed (x,y) while actually moving.

Type 2 – Constant Offset: attacker broadcasts position = real_pos + fixed offset (Δx, Δy).

Type 4 – Random Position: attacker broadcasts a uniformly random position in the full map.

Type 8 – Random Offset: attacker broadcasts real_pos + random offset in a bounding box around the true position.

Type 16 – Eventual Stop: behaves normally first, then repeatedly sends the same position (“freezes”).

All your labels come from the ground truth file in VeReMi / Modified VeReMi (there’s a field that encodes attacker type; 0 or missing means normal).

